 "stimulus_html": "<figure id=\"Ch15_fig01\">\n<img src=\"exercises/media/9b62d13444ae88e5.png\" alt=\"The 1972 map shows electoral and popular vote results for the 1972 presidential election. Every state except Massachusetts, Washington D.C., and part of Virginia supported the Republican candidate Nixon. Massachusetts and D.C. supported the Democratic candidate McGovern. Part of Virginia supported the Libertarian candidate Hospers. Nixon won 96.6% of the electoral vote (520 out of 538 votes) and 60.7% of the popular vote (47,169,911 out of 77,718,554 votes). McGovern won 3.2% of the electoral vote (17 out of 538 votes) and 37.5% of the popular vote (29,170,383 out of 77,718,554 votes). The minor candidate Hospers won 0.2% of the electoral vote (1 out of 538 votes) and 1.8% of the popular vote (1,378,260 out of 77,718,554 votes). Electoral votes by state for Nixon are as follows: Hawaii 4, Alaska 3, Washington 9, Oregon 6, California 45, Nevada 3, Idaho 4, Montana 4, Wyoming 3, Utah 4, Colorado 7, Arizona 6, New Mexico 4, North Dakota 3, South Dakota 4, Nebraska 5, Kansas 7, Oklahoma 8, Texas 26, Minnesota 10, Iowa 8, Missouri 12, Arkansas 6, Louisiana 10, Mississippi 7, Alabama 9, Georgia 12, Florida 17, South Carolina 8, North Carolina 13, Tennessee 11, Kentucky 9, Wisconsin 11, Michigan 21, Illinois 26, Indiana 13, Ohio 25, West Virginia 6, Virginia 11, Maryland 10, Delaware 3, New Jersey 17, Pennsylvania 27, Connecticut 8, New York 41, Rhode Island 4, Vermont 3, New Hampshire 4, Maine 4. Electoral votes by state of McGovern are as follows: Massachusetts 14, D.C. 3. Electoral votes by state for Hospers are Virginia 1.\">\n<figcaption>This map shows the electoral votes won by each candidate in the 1972 presidential election. (credit: “Presidential Electoral Votes Results 1972” by Bill of Rights Institute/Flickr, CC BY 4.0)</figcaption>\n</figure>\n<figure id=\"Ch15_fig02\">\n<img src=\"exercises/media/37eca4ddf02fe4fe.png\" alt=\"The 1976 map shows the electoral and popular vote results for the 1976 election. States supporting the Democratic candidate Carter include Minnesota, Wisconsin, Hawaii, Missouri, Arkansas, Texas, Louisiana, Mississippi, Alabama, Georgia, South Carolina, North Carolina, Tennessee, Kentucky, Ohio, West Virginia, Pennsylvania, Maryland, Washington DC, Delaware, New York, Massachusetts, and Rhode Island. States supporting the Republican candidate Ford include Maine, New Hampshire, Vermont, Connecticut, New Jersey, Virginia, Michigan, Indiana, Illinois, Iowa, Oklahoma, Kansas, Nebraska, South Dakota, North Dakota, Montana, Wyoming, Colorado, New Mexico, Arizona, Utah, Idaho, Nevada, California, Alaska, Oregon, and most of Washington. The eastern part of Washington supported the Republican Candidate Reagan. Carter won 55.2% of the electoral vote (297 out of 538 votes) and 50% of the popular vote (40,830,763 out of 81,555,889 votes). Ford won 44.6% of the electoral vote (240 out of 538 votes) and 48% of the popular vote (39,147,793 out of 81,555,889 votes). Reagan won 0.2% of the electoral vote (1 out of 538 votes) and 2% of the popular vote (1,577,333 out of 81,555,889 votes). Electoral votes by state for Carter are as follows: Hawaii 4, Texas 26, Minnesota 10, Wisconsin 11, Missouri 12, Arkansas 6, Louisiana 10, Mississippi 7, Alabama 9, Georgia 12, Florida 17, South Carolina 8, North Carolina 13, Tennessee 10, Kentucky 9, Ohio 25, West Virginia 6, Washington D.C. 3, Maryland 10, Delaware 3, Pennsylvania 27, New York 41, Massachusetts 14, Rhode Island 4. Electoral votes by state for Ford are as follows: Main 4, New Hampshire 4, Vermont 3, Connecticut 8, New Jersey 17, Virginia 12, Indiana 13, Michigan 21, Illinois 26, Iowa 8, North Dakota 3, South Dakota 4, Nebraska 5, Kansas 7, Oklahoma 8, New Mexico 4, Arizona 6, Utah 4, Colorado 7, Wyoming 3, Montana 4, Idaho 4, Oregon 6, Washington 8, Nevada 3, California 45, Alaska 3. Electoral votes by state for Reagan are as follows: Washington, 1.\">\n<figcaption>This map shows the electoral votes won by each candidate in the 1976 presidential election. Though he did not receive the Republican nomination, Ronald Reagan did receive one vote in the electoral college. (credit: “Presidential Electoral Votes Results 1976” by Bill of Rights Institute/Flickr, CC BY 4.0)</figcaption>\n</figure>\n<p><i>Refer to the maps provided.</i></p>\n",
